Key Concepts Learned
IP Addressing
Every device connected to a network requires a unique address to send and receive information. Understanding device addressing is essential for network analysis and security investigations.

Network Interfaces
Network interfaces allow systems to communicate with other devices across a network. Examining interfaces helps identify how devices connect and exchange data.

DNS
Domain Name System (DNS) allows human-readable website names to be translated into numerical addresses that computers use for communication.

Network Connectivity
Testing connectivity helps verify whether two devices can successfully communicate across a network.

Ports and Services
Applications and services use ports to communicate across networks. Understanding ports is important when performing network analysis and security assessments.

Key Learning Outcomes
During this lab session, I gained practical experience exploring network configuration information within Kali Linux and learned how devices communicate across a network. I developed a stronger understanding of IP addresses, network interfaces, routing, DNS resolution, and connectivity testing. These concepts form the foundation for future cybersecurity activities such as network scanning, traffic analysis, and security monitoring.

Reflection
Today I focused on the networking concepts that support cybersecurity operations. By exploring network configuration information and testing connectivity, I developed a better understanding of how systems communicate and how network information can be identified and analyzed. This knowledge will be used in future labs involving Nmap, Wireshark, and security monitoring tools.
